--- body ---
## Context
Found 2026-11-09 during the claims rollout (JETP-observer PR #285; the 0216 dogfood had hit the same rule in
chemin-de-voix, ticket 0219). The managed pre-commit block refuses a commit staging `tickets/erg` on any branch
but the default one, with "CI rebuilds the binary after merge". That reason holds in git-erg only, where
rebuild-binary.yml commits the binary on main. An adopter vendors the binary by `erg sync` and lands it by pull
request, as integration.md's upgrade recipe says; agents there work on branches and never commit to main. So in
every adopter that installed the hooks, each binary refresh, the claims migration included, needs
`--no-verify`, which also skips the claims index check the same block runs.

## Decision
The author, 2026-11-09: drop the rule from the managed block. git-erg needs no replacement: its CI rebuilds the
binary on main after every merge whatever a pull request carried.

## Exit criteria
- [x] The managed pre-commit block (install.go hookBody) no longer inspects `tickets/erg`; a rerun of
      `erg install --hooks` replaces an installed block in place, so adopters pick up the change.
- [x] integration.md's snippet and prose, `erg install --help` and docs/erg-manual.md no longer state the rule.
- [x] Tests: the rule's tests are removed, and one test shows a hook-installed repo commits `tickets/erg` on a
      feature branch.
- [x] CHANGELOG notes the change.
- [x] Bundled, same rollout: README and CHANGELOG name the import command for a binary older than `sync`
      (`ERG_UPDATE_URL=... tickets/erg update`), the gap padme and JETP-observer hit on 2026-11-09.
- [x] make check passes.
